// Generated by tools/start_here.py from the app's own first-run note: the Start here guide.
window.START = {"title": "Start here", "blocks": [{"kind": "title", "text": "Start here"}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Inkling is a notebook that asks. You write, and it reads along. When a line doesn’t add up, it pulls a thread from those words into the margin: a question, or a correction. It never writes your notes for you. The thinking stays yours."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Everything on this page works. Point at a tag in the margin to read it, click it to answer, and drag it anywhere you like."}, {"kind": "h2", "text": "Threads"}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Reading a 20 GB disk image at 400 MB/s takes 5 seconds."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Restoring a snapshot is always faster than booting."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "A × on a tag is a correction and a ? is a question. Open questions are numbered in reading order, with a knot beside their paragraph, and ⌥⌘↓ jumps to the next one. Fix the words a thread is about and Inkling reads them again; if the problem is gone, the thread ties itself off and its knot joins the border at the top of the page."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Open a tag to write back, and the mind answers in the same thread. Resolve ties it off. Dismiss snips it, and Undo or ⌥⌘Z brings it back. Copy takes the whole thread with you, and Make a note turns it into a note of its own."}, {"kind": "h2", "text": "Reading along"}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Inkling reads each paragraph when you pause, and a small stitch in the gutter marks what it has read. Most of the time it says nothing. A question that comes while you are mid-sentence waits, folded, until you stop."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Tell Inkling, above the title, says what a note is for, and every read takes it into account. Beside it, Reads along can become Waits to be asked: then Inkling stays quiet until you call it, select words, or open the chat."}, {"kind": "h2", "text": "Asking"}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Select some words and a small menu appears. Find a loose thread (⌘↵) picks the one thing in them most worth a question. Ask Inkling takes your own question. Sketch it answers with a drawing, stitched out step by step; click a sketch to see it large. The same menu turns a line into a heading, a list, a quote, a callout or code."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "A warm pool of ten VMs per host is enough for Monday mornings."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Ask the room to hear from up to three minds at once. Each answers on its own thread, in its own colour. Or start a sentence with a mind’s name and a comma, and that mind answers you there."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Firmware, the kernel and the services start side by side, so a boot takes as long as the slowest of them."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "⌘J opens a chat about the whole note. It has read every thread as well, so it can tell you what you have settled and what is still open."}, {"kind": "h2", "text": "Checklists, callouts and code"}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Start a line with [ ] and a space for a checklist item; click its box, or press ⌘L, to check it off. Start one with > [!note], > [!warning] or > [!tip] and a space for a callout. Three backticks and a language, then Return, start a block of code; Return twice at its end leaves it. Inkling reads all of them like any paragraph, and can ask about a single line of code."}, {"kind": "check-done", "text": "Time one cold start with systemd-analyze"}, {"kind": "check", "text": "Restore one VM from a snapshot, nothing else"}, {"kind": "callout-tip", "text": "Time cold starts at p99, not the average: the slow ones are the ones people notice."}, {"kind": "code-rust", "text": "fn boot_ms(firmware: u32, kernel: u32, services: u32) -> u32 {"}, {"kind": "code-rust", "text": "    firmware + kernel + services // one after another"}, {"kind": "code-rust", "text": "}"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "The fastest boot is the one you skip."}, {"kind": "h2", "text": "Minds"}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "The name above the title is the note’s mind. Inkling comes with Staff engineer, Editor, Skeptic, Socratic tutor and Investor. In Settings, under Minds, you can make your own: say what it is for and how it thinks, give it a voice (plain, warm, blunt or Socratic), and choose how often it speaks. Each mind keeps its own thread colour, so you can see who asked what."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Settings, under About you, holds what Inkling knows about you. Turn on Inkling learns about you, and it keeps what matters from your replies."}, {"kind": "h2", "text": "Your notebook"}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "⌘\\ opens your notes and folders; a dot marks notes with open threads. ⌘K finds a note or starts one. ⇧⌘C copies a note, and ⇧⌘E exports it as Markdown, HTML or Word, with its threads or without."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Coming from Obsidian? File > Import from Obsidian brings a vault in with its folders. Inkling leaves the imported words alone, so it reads only what you write afterwards."}, {"kind": "h2", "text": "Make it yours"}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "In Settings (⌘,) choose Light, Dark or the system’s look, the text size, the lettering, and your thread colour: madder, indigo, sage, rose, plum, walnut or ochre. Questions can appear in both margins, in the right margin only, or as small marks in the text. Reading pace can be regular or slow. Ink from the pointer lets a drop of ink fall now and then as you move it."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Hold ⌥ on its own to speak instead of typing. Under Model, pick which Claude model Inkling uses, and how much effort it spends reading along and answering. It runs on the Claude login already on this Mac."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Under Shortcuts you can change any key: click it and press the keys you want."}, {"kind": "h2", "text": "Quiet when you want it"}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "The window’s controls fade while you write and come back when you move the pointer. ⇧⌘. hides every thread and leaves just your words."}, {"kind": "h2", "text": "Keys"}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "⌘↵ finds a loose thread in what you selected."}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "⌥⌘↓ and ⌥⌘↑ move between open threads."}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "⇧⌘⌫ dismisses the open thread, and ⌥⌘Z brings it back."}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "⇧⌘. hides every thread and leaves just your words."}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "⌘J opens a chat about the whole note."}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "⌘L checks or unchecks a checklist item."}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "⌘K finds a note, or starts one."}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "⌘\\ shows your notes and folders."}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "⇧⌘C copies the note, and ⇧⌘E exports it."}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Hold ⌥ to speak instead of typing."}, {"kind": "bullet", "text": "⌘, opens Settings."}, {"kind": "h2", "text": "Your turn"}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Write one sentence below about something you’re working on, or something you believe. Inkling will read it and ask you about it."}, {"kind": "paragraph", "text": ""}], "threads": [{"kind": "correction", "side": "right", "mind_name": "Inkling", "quote": "takes 5 seconds", "drawing": null, "messages": [{"role": "mind", "text": "At 400 MB/s, 20 GB takes 50 seconds. Reading it in 5 needs 4 GB/s. Change the number in the sentence and this thread ties itself off."}]}, {"kind": "question", "side": "left", "mind_name": "Inkling", "quote": "Restoring a snapshot is always faster than booting.", "drawing": null, "messages": [{"role": "mind", "text": "Always? A restore skips the boot, but a guest that has to fault in most of its memory can end up slower than a lean boot. Which have you timed?"}]}, {"kind": "ask", "side": "right", "mind_name": "Skeptic", "quote": "A warm pool of ten VMs per host is enough for Monday mornings.", "drawing": null, "messages": [{"role": "you", "text": "Is this enough?"}, {"role": "mind", "text": "Enough for which minute? A pool sized for the average empties in the first seconds of a burst. How many starts does one host see at nine on a Monday, and how fast does the pool refill?"}]}, {"kind": "ask", "side": "right", "mind_name": "Socratic tutor", "quote": "A warm pool of ten VMs per host is enough for Monday mornings.", "drawing": null, "messages": [{"role": "you", "text": "Is this enough?"}, {"role": "mind", "text": "If twenty requests reach one host in the same second, what happens to the eleventh? What would you measure to find out?"}]}, {"kind": "correction", "side": "left", "mind_name": "Inkling", "quote": "Firmware, the kernel and the services start side by side, so a boot takes as long as the slowest of them.", "drawing": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 176\">\n<g data-step=\"1\" data-caption=\"Firmware runs first, then hands over to the kernel.\">\n<path d=\"M20 96 L300 96\" stroke=\"graphite\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<path d=\"M294 92 L300 96 L294 100\" stroke=\"graphite\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"113\" class=\"sans\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"faint\" text-anchor=\"end\">time</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"44\" width=\"78\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\" stroke=\"ink\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<text x=\"59\" y=\"32\" class=\"voice\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"ink\" text-anchor=\"middle\">firmware</text>\n</g>\n<g data-step=\"2\" data-caption=\"The kernel starts systemd, and only then do the services begin.\">\n<rect x=\"102\" y=\"44\" width=\"58\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\" stroke=\"ink\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<text x=\"131\" y=\"32\" class=\"voice\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"ink\" text-anchor=\"middle\">kernel</text>\n<rect x=\"164\" y=\"44\" width=\"132\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\" stroke=\"ink\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<text x=\"230\" y=\"32\" class=\"voice\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"ink\" text-anchor=\"middle\">services</text>\n<path d=\"M100 76 L100 92 M162 76 L162 92\" stroke=\"faint\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/>\n</g>\n<g data-step=\"3\" data-caption=\"So a boot is the three added up, not the slowest of them.\">\n<path d=\"M20 118 Q20 128 30 128 L148 128 Q158 128 158 138 Q158 128 168 128 L286 128 Q296 128 296 118\" stroke=\"ink\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<text x=\"158\" y=\"162\" class=\"voice\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"ink\" text-anchor=\"middle\">boot = all three, in turn</text>\n</g>\n</svg>", "messages": [{"role": "mind", "text": "They run one after another: firmware hands over to the kernel, the kernel starts systemd, and systemd brings up the services. The times add up. Which of the three takes longest on yours?"}]}]};
